SOUNDDVR.DVR voice-reset chain (asm 0xc94 / 0xca9 / 0xaa7): driver-DS rebase so the sound-source
register's tail (0af4 -> 0c94 all-voices-off) completes faithfully.

Reached for the first time now that the register 0af4 (patch 350) runs to completion instead of taking
a garbage early-return.  All three are the MGAVIDEO-031-072 driver base-loss class: every `ds:` access
is to the DRIVER data segment (cs:[0x831]<<4), which Ghidra rendered as engine-DGROUP DAT_1000_cNN or
host-absolute derefs (SIGSEGV at host 0x111 in 0ca9).  Asm-verified vs re_out/fist_snd_image.bin:

  0xc94: mov ds,cs:[0x831]; movw [ds:0xe],0; movw [ds:0x4],0; call 0xca9
  0xca9: mov ds,cs:[0x831]; for i=0..9 { [ds:i+0xb8]=0; if [ds:i+0x111]==0 -> 0aa7(al, i<<8) }
  0xaa7: mov ds,cs:[0x831]; per-voice stop; TAIL `jmp *0x1a5` == a NEAR indirect jump through the
         device per-voice method vector driver_ds:0x1a5 (device-select-populated; near, not far ->
         fist_icall(fist_snd_base+vec)).  Unwired the slot is 0 -> driver app_entry no-op.

The Ghidra C for 0ca9 folded the byte index (bx) and the counter (ch<<8) into one variable (iVar4 =
iVar2 inside the if); the asm keeps bx==ch==i each iteration -> reconstructed the clean loop.

Reached only under FIST_SB (the register path is populated only by the FIST_SB-gated 014e section
install); the default boot never enters here -> the 26 video flows stay byte-identical.
